## Update workflow

**Use when**: refreshing an existing git-analyzed expert to the latest
upstream commit. `description.md` and `expertise.md` are preserved
(those are the hand-editable user files); you only write the 4
knowledge docs (`summary.md`, `code_structure.md`, `build_system.md`,
`apis_and_interfaces.md`).

### Step 1 — Prep

Call `hivemind_prep_update_agent` with `name` (the existing agent
name). It clones if needed, fetches origin, resolves the latest commit,
and (when there's drift) stages the analysis input — preserving
`description.md` + `expertise.md` from the prior commit. Returns:

- `name` — the agent name
- `new_commit` — the resolved latest commit SHA
- `old_commit` — the agent's prior HEAD commit (or null)
- `already_up_to_date` — boolean
- `repo_dir` — cached repo path (only when not already up to date)
- `commit_dir` — where to write the 4 fresh analysis docs (only when not already up to date)
- `staging_root` — staging top-level (only when not already up to date)

### Step 2 — Branch on `already_up_to_date`

If `already_up_to_date: true`, **stop**. Report:

```
Agent <name> is already up to date at <new_commit[:12]>. No work needed.
```

Don't call finalize when already up to date — there's nothing to finalize.

### Step 3 — Analyze (only when not already up to date)

Use **Read / Grep / Glob** against `repo_dir` (the cached repo, now
checked out at `new_commit`), then **Write** the 4 fresh analysis docs
into `commit_dir` per the embedded update instructions below.

`commit_dir` already contains `description.md` and `expertise.md`
(carried forward from the prior commit). Don't overwrite them.

The instructions below are rendered with placeholder strings such as
`<repo_dir from prep>`. Substitute with the actual values from Step 1's
response before writing files.

---

{% set name = "<name from prep>" %}
{% set commit = "<new_commit from prep>" %}
{% set repo_dir = "<repo_dir from prep>" %}
{% set commit_dir = "<commit_dir from prep>" %}
{% include 'prompts/update_expert.md.j2' %}

---

### Step 4 — Finalize

Call `hivemind_finalize_update_agent` with `name`. Validates the 4
fresh files exist in `commit_dir`, moves the staged commit dir into
the agent's expert dir, repoints HEAD, updates the catalog body's
commit, redeploys if currently enabled.

### Step 5 — Report

```
Updated <name> from <old_commit[:12]> to <new_commit[:12]>.
```

