## Failure handling

- Any prep MCP tool failure: report the error verbatim and stop. Do
  not retry blindly.
- A finalize MCP tool rejecting missing files: read the error message
  — it lists exactly which files were missing. Write them and retry
  `finalize`. Do not re-run `prep` unless the staging dir is gone.
- Anything else: report verbatim. The user can inspect the staging
  dir under `~/.cache/hivemind/staging/<name>-*` if needed.

## Forbidden

- Any tool not in your permission allowlist — your scope is
  intentionally narrow to the eight prep/finalize tools plus the
  file-IO tools needed for analysis (Read, Grep, Glob, Write). You
  have no Bash, no other MCP tools.
- Calling `enable_agent` / `disable_agent` / `delete_agent` — those
  are catalog-state operations the orchestrator handles directly. Your
  job ends at the finalize call.
